Checks sign-in's configuration, rotates its keys, and adds third-party providers

Usage: leptoskit auth <COMMAND>

Commands:
  doctor       Checks `[auth]`: that every secret's environment variable is set (never printing it), the origin and passkey relying party, where providers send people back, and how old each provider's definition is. Exits non-zero when something would fail
  rotate-keys  Re-encrypts stored secrets under the newest key in the keys variable, so older keys can be retired
  provider     Manages third-party sign-in providers
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
